WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.155
Four ways to build an agent with Claude.

2
00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:06.893
Anthropic offers four routes, and two of them have confusingly similar names.

3
00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:16.347
Two questions separate them: who supplies the harness (the loop and context management) and who supplies the deployment (where the agent and its tools run).

4
00:00:16.627 --> 00:00:18.397
Plain code, the manual loop.

5
00:00:18.677 --> 00:00:22.795
You call the Messages API and write the loop yourself, as in the lab.

6
00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:24.909
You own the harness and the hosting.

7
00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:27.792
Maximum control, no beta dependency.

8
00:00:28.072 --> 00:00:29.139
The tool runner.

9
00:00:29.419 --> 00:00:32.704
A helper in the regular anthropic SDK ( client.

10
00:00:32.984 --> 00:00:33.816
beta.

11
00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:35.013
messages.

12
00:00:35.293 --> 00:00:38.323
tool_runner in Python, with @beta_tool functions).

13
00:00:38.603 --> 00:00:48.373
It runs the request, execute, repeat cycle for tools you define, wraps tool exceptions as is_error results, and stops at max_iterations if you set it.

14
00:00:48.653 --> 00:00:52.429
It has no built-in tools, no filesystem, and no sandbox.

15
00:00:52.709 --> 00:00:53.648
You host it.

16
00:00:53.928 --> 00:01:05.960
The tool runner docs suggest the manual loop when you need human approval, custom logging, or conditional execution, although the SDK also exposes per-iteration hooks for some of this.

17
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.968
The Claude Agent SDK.

18
00:01:08.248 --> 00:01:15.736
A separate package ( claude-agent-sdk for Python, @anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk for TypeScript).

19
00:01:16.016 --> 00:01:22.928
It is Claude Code as a library, renamed from the Claude Code SDK in September 2025.

20
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:39.635
You call query() with a prompt and options, and it drives the full Claude Code harness: built-in tools for reading, writing, and editing files, running shell commands, and searching, plus hooks, permissions, sessions, subagents, MCP, and automatic compaction.

21
00:01:39.915 --> 00:01:41.109
You still host it.

22
00:01:41.389 --> 00:01:48.280
Claude Managed Agents (beta, header managed-agents-2026-04-01 ).

23
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.184
Anthropic runs the harness and the deployment.

24
00:01:51.464 --> 00:02:06.205
You create an agent (model, system prompt, tools, MCP servers, skills) once, then start sessions in an environment, either an Anthropic-managed cloud sandbox or a self-hosted sandbox, and exchange events with it.

25
00:02:06.485 --> 00:02:09.515
It suits long-running, asynchronous, and scheduled work.

26
00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:12.461
The tool runner is not the Agent SDK.

27
00:02:12.741 --> 00:02:20.933
One is a thin loop over your tools inside the client SDK; the other is a batteries-included coding and filesystem agent.

28
00:02:21.213 --> 00:02:23.091
Both run on your infrastructure.

29
00:02:23.371 --> 00:02:25.355
Only Managed Agents is hosted.
